 ## Overview
-VolumeSlice Repaint is a client-side JavaScript method for rendering a single volumetric slice onto an HTML5 Canvas by directly manipulating pixel data. It solves the problem of visualizing scalar or label volumetric data in a web browser without requiring WebGL shaders for the final compositing step, relying instead on CPU-based pixel manipulation. It differs from GPU-accelerated texture slicing (such as [Sliced Volume Rendering](3568-sliced-volume-rendering.md)) by performing the transfer function application and alpha compositing on the CPU, which allows for simpler integration with standard DOM elements but limits performance to the speed of JavaScript execution and canvas buffer access.
+VolumeSlice Repaint is a client-side JavaScript method that renders a single volumetric slice onto an HTML5 Canvas by directly manipulating pixel data [S1, unofficial]. It visualizes scalar or label volumetric data in a web browser using CPU-based pixel manipulation instead of WebGL shaders for the final compositing step [S1, unofficial].
 
